silm:instances_papers_15_chapters_01_sections_01_concrete_anchor_cocone_leg_n_plus_1 a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "ConcreteAnchorCoconeLegStageNplus1Example" .
silm:instances_papers_15_chapters_01_sections_01_concrete_anchor_cocone_leg_n_plus_1 silm:hasExample "In 'ConcreteAnchorCoconeLegStageNplus1', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, For l=BodyMassQuality77 and n+1=2, the cocone leg is the SAME arrow as at stage 1 (the body-mass attachment to Mittens). The microchip-read event does not modify this arrow; it adds a different arrow (MicrochipIdentifier9 -> Mittens) beside it.." .
